# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# OpenClaw agent-workspace scaffolding — NOT part of the website. Default
# boilerplate an OpenClaw run drops in its working dir; deleted 2026-06-23 and
# ignored here so a future run in this repo can't re-add them. Also ignore the
# stray flock-profiles JSON backups agents leave behind.
/.openclaw/
/.openclaw-cli-images/
/AGENTS.md
/HEARTBEAT.md
/IDENTITY.md
/SOUL.md
/TOOLS.md
/USER.md
/content/flock-profiles.json.bak.*

# Reel MP4s are transport, not content (01-Aug-2026). They exist only so Meta
# can fetch each one once during container ingest; nothing on this site links
# to a .mp4. They are served from the Mini instead —
# guardian.markbarney.net/api/v1/images/reel-assets/<name>.mp4 — and swept
# after 48h. Committing them had banked 346 clips / 3.9 GB in git history.
# See docs/01-Aug-2026-reel-hosting-remediation-plan.md
/public/photos/reels/

# Story JPEGs are the same case as the reels above, and were simply never
# given the same treatment (15-Aug-2026). Same reasoning applies verbatim:
# transport, not content. They existed only so Meta could fetch each one once
# during story ingest; stories expire after 24h and nothing on this site has
# ever linked to one. Serving moved to the Mini on 04-May-2026 —
# guardian.markbarney.net/api/v1/images/story-assets/<name>.jpg — and the
# assets are swept after 48h. The lane stopped writing here that same day;
# CLAUDE.md has called this directory "a frozen archive" ever since, while
# 334 files / 111 MB stayed in git.
#
# NOTE the leading slash: this must NOT match the archive lane's still-active
# public/photos/on-this-day/YYYY-MM-DD/stories/, which is a different tree.
/public/photos/stories/
